#. name of box generator
#: boxes/generators/coinbanksafe.py
msgid "CoinBankSafe"
msgstr "Salvadanaio cassaforte"

#. description of CoinBankSafe
#: boxes/generators/coinbanksafe.py
msgid "A piggy-bank designed to look like a safe."
msgstr "Un salvadanaio a forma di cassaforte."

#. long description of CoinBankSafe in markdown
#: boxes/generators/coinbanksafe.py
msgid ""
"\n"
"Make sure not to discard the circle cutouts from the lid, base, and door. "
"They are all needed.\n"
"\n"
"![Closed](static/samples/CoinBankSafe-closed.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"![Open](static/samples/CoinBankSafe-open.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"Assemble the locking pins like this: wiggle-disc, number-disc, doorhole-"
"disc, spacer-disc, D-disc.\n"
"Glue the first three in place, but do not glue the last two.\n"
"Leaving them unglued will allow you change the code, and to remove the pin "
"from the door.\n"
"\n"
"![Pins](static/samples/CoinBankSafe-pins.jpg)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Non buttare i dischi ritagliati dal coperchio, dalla base e dallo sportello: "
"servono tutti.\n"
"\n"
"![Chiuso](static/samples/CoinBankSafe-closed.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"![Aperto](static/samples/CoinBankSafe-open.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"Monta i perni di chiusura in quest'ordine: disco ondulato, disco numerato, "
"disco del foro dello sportello, disco distanziale, disco a D.\n"
"Incolla i primi tre, ma non gli ultimi due.\n"
"Lasciandoli senza colla potrai cambiare la combinazione e sfilare il perno "
"dallo sportello.\n"
"\n"
"![Perni](static/samples/CoinBankSafe-pins.jpg)\n"
"\n"

